  {"q":"What should a plumber's invoice include?","a":"Your business and licence details, the client and job address, an itemised split of labour, parts and any call-out or emergency fee, tax if registered, a clear total and payment details."},
  {"q":"Should I charge a call-out fee?","a":"It's common to, especially for emergencies or out-of-hours work. Show it as its own line so the client sees what the fee covers, which makes it far easier to accept."},
  {"q":"Should I take a deposit on big plumbing jobs?","a":"For larger jobs with upfront material costs, yes &mdash; a deposit covers parts and the balance is due on completion. For quick call-outs, invoicing in full on the day is usually fine."},
