  {"h2":"Bill by headcount and menu","html":"<p>Most catering is priced <b>per head for a chosen menu</b>, so state the per-person price, the guest count, and the menu clearly. Add-ons &mdash; drinks packages, extra courses, dietary options &mdash; go on their own lines so the total is easy to follow.</p>"},
  {"h2":"Staff, rentals and delivery","html":"<p>List <b>service staff, equipment rental, delivery and setup</b> separately from the food. Clients want to see what&rsquo;s food and what&rsquo;s service, and separating them makes the invoice transparent and easier to approve.</p>"},
  {"h2":"Final numbers and cancellation","html":"<p>Guest numbers move, so agree a <b>cut-off date for final headcount</b> and state that the invoice is based on the confirmed figure. Put your <b>cancellation and final-numbers terms</b> in writing up front, so the final invoice holds no surprises for either side.</p>"},
